摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"DSH plug -- cli coding agent with Minimal/Router profiles, [Windows] support, MCP, agents, and a polished TUI.","id":"gh:1333955987","install_available":false,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dhs-tuicode","slug":"BenHuHuan/dhs-tuicode","topics":["cli","coding-agent","deepseek","dsh-plugin","dsh-terminal","dsh-tui","mcp","tui","typescript"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"DSH plug -- cli coding agent with Minimal/Router profiles, [Windows] support, MCP, agents, and a pol"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"- cli coding agent with Minimal/Router profiles, [Windows] support, MCP, agents, and a polished TUI."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# DeepSeek Code TUI"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"[](https://github.com/BenHuHuan/dhs-tuicode/tree/v0.3.0) [](https://github.com/BenHuHuan/dhs-tuicode"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"thub.com/BenHuHuan/dhs-tuicode/tree/v0.3.0) [](https://github.com/BenHuHuan/dhs-tuicode) [](LICENSE)"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"**DeepSeek Code TUI** is a terminal-native coding agent built on the official DeepSeek Harness. It c"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"ombines DeepSeek V4 Pro/Flash, a persistent TUI, real coding tools, resumable sessions, permissions,"},{"id":"p5s3","text":" MCP, skills, and continuable subagents in one shell-first workflow."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Run `deepseek` inside a project. No browser is required."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"> This is an independent community distribution. It is not an official DeepSeek product and is not a"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"ffiliated with Anthropic. Claude Code is referenced only as a terminal UX comparison."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## Why this build"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"- **DeepSeek-native defaults:** V4 Pro, max reasoning effort, and a Minimal first request that revea"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"ls the complete coding tool catalog on demand. The catalog also includes the vision-capable `deepsee"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"k-v4-flash-vision-exp` model for image input.\n- **Real Bash semantics on Windows:** model-facing she"},{"id":"p9s4","text":"ll calls use Git Bash/MSYS instead of pretending PowerShell is Bash; safe Windows operations can sti"},{"id":"p9s5","text":"ll use PowerShell.\n- **A complete terminal loop:** inspect, search, edit, run commands, review diffs"},{"id":"p9s6","text":", create checkpoints, rewind, resume, export, and manage long-running work without leaving the TUI.\n"},{"id":"p9s7","text":"- **Explicit safety states:** permission and planning modes have distinct colors, prompt rails, glyp"},{"id":"p9s8","text":"hs, and footer labels; unrestricted access is always an explicit choice.\n- **Extensible by design:**"},{"id":"p9s9","text":" MCP servers, skills, durable subagents, and the `allin` multi-agent tool use the underlying Cordis "},{"id":"p9s10","text":"plugin architecture rather than a separate wrapper runtime.\n- **Windows-friendly interaction:** CJK-"},{"id":"p9s11","text":"aware layout, mouse scrolling, jump-to-bottom, selection copy, multiline paste blocks, clipboard ima"},{"id":"p9s12","text":"ges, and width-safe rendering."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## v0.3.0 highlights"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"- **Vision prompts:** select `deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp` with `/model` to send text, clipboard im"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"ages, or both in one prompt.\n- **Reliable Windows image paste:** Alt+V reads native PNG bytes, bitma"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"p clipboard objects, and copied image files; Ctrl+V also works when the terminal forwards that chord"},{"id":"p11s4","text":" to the TUI.\n- **Composable drafts:** image markers stay in place beside ordinary text and multiline"},{"id":"p11s5","text":" paste blocks, while text-only bracketed paste replays unchanged.\n- **Safe admission:** image bytes "},{"id":"p11s6","text":"remain draft-local until send, and text-only model routes reject image prompts before attachment per"},{"id":"p11s7","text":"aft-local until send, and text-only model routes reject image prompts before attachment persistence."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"### Requirements"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"- Node.js `22.19+` or `24+` (Node 24 recommended)\n- pnpm `11.7+`\n- Git and a DeepSeek API key\n- Wind"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"ows Terminal, WezTerm, Kitty, iTerm2, or another modern terminal\n- Git for Windows when using the Ba"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"sh-backed profiles on Windows"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"### Install from source"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"The current source line is **v0.3.0**. Packaged installers and npm releases are not available yet."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"Open a new terminal, enter a project, and run:"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"To run directly from a checkout without the global link:"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"On Windows, the built repository-local entry is:"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"### First session"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"1. Run `deepseek` in the directory you want the agent to edit.\n2. Enter `/login` and paste the DeepS"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"eek API key. The credential provider saves it for later sessions.\n3. Use `/model` to confirm or chan"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"ge the model.\n4. Enter a coding request and press Enter.\n5. Press Shift+Tab to change the active per"},{"id":"p25s4","text":"mission/planning state."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"For a one-off unrestricted launch:"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"## What is included"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"| Area | Capabilities |"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"| Coding | File read/search/edit, shell execution, background jobs, task lists, tool cards, external"},{"id":"p31s2","text":" editor, and direct `! command` execution |\n| Sessions | Persistent logs, resume/continue, rename, c"},{"id":"p31s3","text":"lear/new, prompt history, context compaction, copy, and export |\n| Review and recovery | Interactive"},{"id":"p31s4","text":" diff, named workspace/conversation checkpoints, rewind, and conversation branching |\n| Models | Pro"},{"id":"p31s5","text":"vider/model selection, reasoning effort, thinking visibility, token usage, vision image input, image"},{"id":"p31s6","text":" token estimation, and context pressure |\n| Extensions | MCP status/reload, skill discovery and invo"},{"id":"p31s7","text":"cation, durable subagent management, and Cordis plugins |\n| Multi-agent | `allin` orchestration with"},{"id":"p31s8","text":" a V4 Pro coordinator and parallel V4 Flash execution lanes |\n| Terminal UX | Mouse scrolling, jump-"},{"id":"p31s9","text":"to-bottom, OSC 52 selection copy, inline paste blocks, clipboard-image input, terminal images, ANSI "},{"id":"p31s10","text":"pixel fallback, and CJK-aware width handling |"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"## Local data and security"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"- Sessions, configuration, and managed credentials are stored under the configured DSH home director"},{"id":"p33s2","text":"y.\n- `/status` and normal logs do not print the saved API key.\n- Workspace Write is the normal editi"},{"id":"p33s3","text":"ng authority; Inspect and Plan reduce mutation authority; bypass removes approval prompts.\n- Use `/c"},{"id":"p33s4","text":"heckpoint` before broad refactors, but keep using Git and backups: rewind is not transactional stora"},{"id":"p33s5","text":"ge.\n- Do not grant unrestricted access to an untrusted repository."},{"id":"p34s1","text":"## Architecture and extension points"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"DeepSeek Code remains a DeepSeek Harness distribution rather than a monolithic wrapper. Cordis plugi"},{"id":"p35s2","text":"ns provide model routes, tools, sessions, permissions, credentials, MCP, skills, agents, and the TUI"},{"id":"p35s3","text":". Optional capabilities can be added or removed without replacing the core agent loop."},{"id":"p36s1","text":"- Architecture\n- TUI subsystem\n- MCP subsystem\n- Skills subsystem\n- Development guide\n- Testing guid"},{"id":"p36s2","text":" Architecture\n- TUI subsystem\n- MCP subsystem\n- Skills subsystem\n- Development guide\n- Testing guide"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"## Current limitations"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"- Installation is source-based; there is no npm, MSI, Homebrew, or standalone binary release yet.\n- "},{"id":"p38s2","text":"Mouse reporting, OSC 52 clipboard support, color, fonts, and image protocols vary by terminal.\n- MCP"},{"id":"p38s3","text":", skills, and agents have functional terminal management surfaces rather than graphical marketplaces"},{"id":"p38s4","text":".\n- Checkpoints support local coding recovery but do not replace commits, worktrees, or backups.\n- C"},{"id":"p38s5","text":"onfiguration and compatibility may change before v1.0."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
